menu "LZ4 Configurations"

    config LZ4_USE_PSRAM
        bool "Prefer PSRAM for LZ4 internal allocations"
        default n
        help
            Prefer PSRAM for LZ4 Block and HC compression workspaces when
            available. Internal 8-bit RAM is used as a fallback when PSRAM is not
            initialized or cannot satisfy an allocation.

            This option enables LZ4_USER_MEMORY_FUNCTIONS. It affects allocations
            made by the Block and HC implementations. Frame APIs use their own
            custom-memory interface; use LZ4F_createCompressionContext_advanced()
            or LZ4F_createDecompressionContext_advanced() when Frame allocations
            must use a specific memory region. This option does not move
            application-owned input, output, or explicitly allocated streaming
            states automatically.

endmenu
